      "id": "2120144623150473649",
      "text": "The other thing I’ll say about $hg $hgraf is once the orders start, I expect the numbers of people trying to make these sorts of tables to rise dramatically.  It will go from a story with little doubts other than how many tonnes will it ultimately sell and in how many products and industries.\n\nWhen I first started writing about the company and interviewing management last summer there were considerable hurdles that needed to be achieved, permits to produce and sell, capital for factory buildout,  ability to get a pipeline gas feed, along with the customer evaluations. \n\nA year and a bit later there is the company really just has the major hurdle of converting evaluators to purchasing clients.  The best part is we’ve been told that the evaluations have been proceeding extremely well.  They haven’t lost a potential customer and the time lag to orders has been mainly manufacturing process related, mixing, time, temp, and testing of products (like getting paints certified, or plastics strength tested) we’ve also heard the companies like the top 10 automaker was hoping for a ~10% improvement in light weighting plastics and they delivered ~30%.   So incredibly significant it’s still hard to truly grasp the value for global plastic industry.  The profound effect this will have (along with recycling improvements, leaching reduction  and uv protection) \n\nA large order from a top 10 automaker will be a fantastic endorsement of the company and the tech.  It will completely change the narrative and the shorts will get completely destroyed. \n\nNot advice do your own due diligence",
